---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Installation">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 prose prose-invert">

    <a href="/docs" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline block mb-6">
      ← Back to documentation
    </a>

    <!-- INSTALLATION CONTENT STARTS HERE -->
    <h1>Installation</h1>

    <p>Desktop‑2FA can be installed on all major platforms.  
    The application is fully offline and requires only Python 3.12+.</p>

    <h2>macOS</h2>

    <h3>Homebrew</h3>
    <pre><code>brew install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h3>pipx</h3>
    <pre><code>pipx install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h3>pip</h3>
    <pre><code>pip install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2>Linux</h2>

    <h3>pipx (recommended)</h3>
    <pre><code>pipx install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h3>pip</h3>
    <pre><code>pip install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h3>From source</h3>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/wrogistefan/desktop-2fa
cd desktop-2fa
pip install .
    </code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2>Windows</h2>

    <h3>pipx (recommended)</h3>
    <pre><code>pipx install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h3>pip</h3>
    <pre><code>pip install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h3>Password file permissions</h3>
    <p>Ensure password files are readable only by your user.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Verify installation</h2>
    <pre><code>python -c "import desktop_2fa; print(desktop_2fa.__version__)"</code></pre>

    <hr />

    <h2>Next steps</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Read the CLI reference</li>
      <li>Learn how the vault works</li>
      <li>Review the security model</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- INSTALLATION CONTENT ENDS HERE -->

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
